    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"2006–2017 dynamics by municipal type\"\nsubtitle: \"Results from the project's Article C, recalculated using the Manuscript 1 types\"\ndescription: \"Change in the number, area and mean area of agricultural establishments between the 2006 and 2017 Censuses, by the five municipal types from Manuscript 1 and by biome\"\ncss: resultados.css\n---\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"faixa-versao\">\nPreliminary version for the project team. Results may change as the study progresses.\n English translation under review. If the two versions differ, the Portuguese text prevails.\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Context and objective\n\nThe project's Article C compared the 2006 and 2017 Agricultural Censuses, both conducted by the Brazilian Institute of Geography and Statistics (IBGE). This page recalculates those results using the **five types from Manuscript 1** (provisional labels) and the dominant biome from the IBGE 1:250,000 map. The aim is to examine how the number, area and mean area of establishments changed in each group.\n\n## Data and methods\n\nThe figures refer to **all agricultural establishments**, not only family farms, in the 141 municipalities of Mato Grosso (MT). Intercensal changes are calculated from the municipal sum for each group. Differences between types and between biomes are assessed with the Kruskal-Wallis test on municipal percentage changes, with no correction for spatial autocorrelation. The municipal sum for the first Census does not reconcile with the state table, as detailed in the box below and in @tbl-conciliacao in the appendix to this page.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"nota-conciliacao\">\n<h4>The 2006 municipal sum does not reconcile with the state table</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>The sum across the 141 municipalities comes to 112,987 establishments and 48.69 million ha in 2006. The 2006–2017 state comparison table records 112,978 establishments and 47.81 million ha, a difference in area of 883 thousand ha (1.8%).</li>\n<li>The IBGE Census comparison table (historical series) records 112,987 establishments and 48,688,710 ha in 2006, figures that match the municipal sum. It is not yet clear why these figures differ from the state table.</li>\n<li>In 2017, the sum reconciles: 118,679 establishments and 54,922,849 ha, against 54,922,850 ha in the state total (a rounding difference).</li>\n<li>The changes shown below use the municipal sum in both years, so that 2006 and 2017 share the same basis.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Value of production: excluded from this version\n\n::: {.callout-warning appearance=\"simple\"}\n**The 2006 value of production does not reconcile.** The state table records R\\$9.60 billion, but the sum from the corrected municipal database (IBGE, table 1118) comes to R\\$12.29 billion, 28% more (2006 values at current prices). Until the difference is explained, the change in the value of production between 2006 and 2017 remains excluded from the website.\n:::\n\n## Change in Mato Grosso\n\nThe cards below summarise the change in the state as a whole.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"kpi-grade\">\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">Agricultural establishments</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">5.0%</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">112,987 in 2006 → 118,679 in 2017 · sum across the 141 municipalities</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">Area of establishments</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">12.8%</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">48.69 → 54.92 million ha · sum across the 141 municipalities</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">Mean area per establishment</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">7.4%</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">431 → 463 ha · ratio of sums</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">Municipalities that lost establishments</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">58 of 141</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">49 of 141 lost area · IBGE, 2006 and 2017 Censuses</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<p class=\"nota-fonte\">Source: authors’ calculations based on IBGE, 2006 and 2017 Agricultural Censuses (SIDRA), all agricultural establishments; municipal database from Article C (corrected version); municipal types from RESA Project Manuscript 1 (provisional labels); dominant biome from the IBGE 1:250,000 map (2019).</p>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Change by type\n\n::: {#tbl-dinamica-tipo}\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"reactable html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-315f3236385894e402f5\" style=\"width:auto;height:auto;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-315f3236385894e402f5\">{\"x\":{\"tag\":{\"name\":\"Reactable\",\"attribs\":{\"data\":{\"Grupo\":[\"<span class=\\\"chip chip-t1\\\">T1 · Low aggregate scale<\\/span>\\n<span class=\\\"rotulo-provisorio\\\" title=\\\"Label pending approval by the authors of Manuscript 1\\\">provisional label<\\/span>\",\"<span class=\\\"chip chip-t2\\\">T2 · Tenure awaiting title, unspecialised<\\/span>\\n<span class=\\\"rotulo-provisorio\\\" title=\\\"Label pending approval by the authors of Manuscript 1\\\">provisional label<\\/span>\",\"<span class=\\\"chip chip-t3\\\">T3 · High aggregate scale<\\/span>\\n<span class=\\\"rotulo-provisorio\\\" title=\\\"Label pending approval by the authors of Manuscript 1\\\">provisional label<\\/span>\",\"<span class=\\\"chip chip-t4\\\">T4 · Mechanised with tenure awaiting title<\\/span>\\n<span class=\\\"rotulo-provisorio\\\" title=\\\"Label pending approval by the authors of Manuscript 1\\\">provisional label<\\/span>\",\"<span class=\\\"chip chip-t5\\\">T5 · Horticultural-irrigated<\\/span>\\n<span class=\\\"rotulo-provisorio\\\" title=\\\"Label pending approval by the authors of Manuscript 1\\\">provisional label<\\/span>\",\"<b>